      "writtenOn": "2023-06-15T04:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I mistyped my previous comment. The bond_state in cancelling/aborting is `BT_BOND_STATE_NONE`\n\nSo the elseif in line 268 should be removed and we could have another block for the cancelling/aborting cases. However, this could be not easy.\nFor canceling from UI, it is`BT_STATUS_AUTH_FAILURE`, `BT_BOND_STATE_NONE` and `hci::ErrorCode::SUCCESS`. For aborting from the remote device, it is `BT_STATUS_FAIL`,`BT_BOND_STATE_NONE` and `hci::ErrorCode::SUCCESS`. Both cases are treated as pair success in the current implementation because hci overwrites bt_status but they should be `PAIR_FAIL_CANCEL`. Translating these 2 cases to `PAIR_FAIL_CANCEL` could hide some real failures.\n\nI also found that reconnecting phonehub has the same combination of forgetting a device (bond_state\u003dnone, the other 2 are success). So I think this could be the major contributor of most pairing_cancel results in our dashboard.\n\nIn conclusion, I think we should not care about canceling/aborting cases for now to react on the low pair success rate issue.",
